    "body": "### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n\r\nOur project is setup with Spring + JOOQ + Kotlin Coroutine + Hikari Data Source, and we tried the below [example](https://www.jooq.org/doc/latest/manual/sql-building/kotlin-sql-building/kotlin-coroutines#NE40A7) provided from official document.\r\n\r\n```kotlin\r\nfun mcveTest() {\r\n  runBlocking {\r\n      ctx.transactionCoroutine { c ->\r\n          c.dsl()\r\n              .insertInto(tableType)\r\n              .set(record)\r\n              .returning()\r\n              .awaitFirst()\r\n          \r\n          throw RuntimeException()\r\n      }  // <---- Should be rollback over here\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n``` \r\n\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nHowever, insert/update statements are committed immediately after awaitFirst() execution, transaction is unable to rollback even an exception is being throw afterward.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce the problem\r\n\r\nCompared the connections populated during \"begin of tx\" and \"execution\". Seems it is unable to reuse the same connection and acquire a new connection.\r\n\r\n### Running with transactionCoroutine\r\n1. Begin Tx (Running in main thread) -> PgConnection@**13844**\r\n<img width=\"1289\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/jOOQ/jOOQ/assets/100355958/2bcdddda-f9f7-4ec2-bfed-b1884b05993d\">\r\n\r\n2. Execute Statement (Running in worker thread) -> PgConnection@**14455**\r\n<img width=\"1308\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/jOOQ/jOOQ/assets/100355958/49b83882-eb1c-4cd3-b2e7-3fc798f44533\">\r\n\r\n### Running with transaction\r\n1. Begin Tx (Running in main thread) -> PgConnection@**13705**\r\n<img width=\"1310\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/jOOQ/jOOQ/assets/100355958/5f279692-55f7-4bf2-9513-50ad8a6448ac\">\r\n\r\n2. Execute Statement (Running in main thread) -> PgConnection@**13705**\r\n<img width=\"1306\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/jOOQ/jOOQ/assets/100355958/b02c6442-6773-4c48-b434-1afe2b7afce2\">\r\n\r\nMCVE: https://github.com/giottcww/jOOQ-mcve\r\n\r\n### jOOQ Version\r\n\r\n3.17.8\r\n\r\n### Database product and version\r\n\r\nPostgreSQL 15.1 (Debian 15.1-1.pgdg110+1)\r\n\r\n### Java Version\r\n\r\nopenjdk version 17\r\n\r\n### OS Version\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### JDBC driver name and version (include name if unofficial driver)\r\n\r\n_No response_",
